<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39104" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-sŭbĭgo</span></b> ,
			ĕre, v. a. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To dig up</i>, <i>cast up</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terram,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 256</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To fashion beforehand</i>, <i>prepare</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fulmina Cyclops Prosubigit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 4, 288</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>To</i>
			
			<i>tear down</i>, <i>trample on</i>:
			molam pede, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 3,
		130.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
